.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
data/raw/*
!data/raw/.gitkeep
results/*
!results/.gitkeep
# Bulk result tables stay out -- they are regenerable and large. These are not:
# the selected configuration that committed code reads by path, the meta files
# that record each run's exact protocol, and the small cohort-quality table the
# README cites. Keeping them tracked is what makes a reported number auditable
# without rerunning three hours of compute.
!results/*_meta.json
!results/*_chosen.json
!results/*_chosen_steprule.json
!results/db3_signal_quality.csv
# The shareable figures and the predictions they are built from. The predictions are
# labels only -- no EMG -- so they carry no redistribution problem, and keeping them
# is what makes every figure reproducible without storing model weights.
!results/visuals/
!results/visuals/**
!results/project_page.html
*.pt
# Vendored third-party render assets and intermediates. The GLB, three.js and the
# licence notices are kept (they are what the figures were made with and the licences
# require the notice to travel); the rendered frames are regenerable and bulky.
assets/render/frames/
assets/three/build/
assets/three/examples/
.DS_Store
results/selfcheck_*
results/pilot_*
